  "final_answer_preview": "According to Section 127(1) of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023, wrongful confinement occurs when a person is wrongfully restrained in such a manner that they cannot proceed beyond certain circumscribing limits. Additionally, Section 127(8) outlines that wrongful confinement for the purpose of extorting confessions or information, or to compel the restoration of property, is punishable by imprisonment for up to three years and a fine.",
